    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Persistence — Service Binary Drop", "technique": "T1543.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-11-14 02:11:08 CET, Wazuh FIM detected a new file creation event under C:\\ProgramData\\winupd_021108\\svc.exe on WIN-SRV-108. The directory winupd_021108 was itself created seconds earlier in %ProgramData% — a non-standard location for service binaries. Legitimate Windows services use %ProgramFiles%, %SystemRoot%\\System32, or vendor-specific signed paths. The binary lacks Authenticode signature. The parent process creating the directory and dropping the file was cmd.exe (not msiexec, not a legitimate software installer). The binary contains an embedded C2 configuration string.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh FIM rule fired on syscheck.path matching *ProgramData* with syscheck.event=added. The creating process chain (cmd.exe → New-Item / [IO.File]::WriteAllBytes) is not consistent with any enterprise software deployment workflow.", "first_seen": "2026-11-14T02:11:08+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Persistence — Service Registration", "technique": "T1543.003", "what_happened": "At 02:12:44 CET, Windows Security Event 7045 fired: a new service named WinUpdateHelper_021108 was installed on WIN-SRV-108. The service binary path (binPath) is C:\\ProgramData\\winupd_021108\\svc.exe — the exact file dropped in Step 1. Service account is LocalSystem (maximum privilege). Start type is auto-start (starts at every boot). The service name WinUpdateHelper typosquats the legitimate Windows Update service to blend into the services list. Event 4697 also fired confirming LocalSystem assignment.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 7045 (New Service Was Installed) with service_file_name=C:\\ProgramData\\winupd_021108\\svc.exe and service_account=LocalSystem. The combination of non-standard binPath path + LocalSystem + auto-start + typosquatting name is the T1543.003 persistence signature. Event 4697 corroborates LocalSystem assignment.", "first_seen": "2026-11-14T02:12:44+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Persistence — FIM Confirmation Hold", "technique": "T1543.003", "what_happened": "Between 02:12:44 and 02:23:41 CET (~11 minutes), the binary C:\\ProgramData\\winupd_021108\\svc.exe and the service registration WinUpdateHelper_021108 persisted on WIN-SRV-108. FIM continued to report the file as present with no modification events. The service remained in auto-start state. No cleanup was attempted during the persistence window — the attacker's binary is durable across reboots via the registered service.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh FIM syscheck.path=C:\\ProgramData\\winupd_021108\\svc.exe shows only 'added' event, no 'modified' or 'deleted' events during the 11-minute hold window. The service is auto-start LocalSystem = survives reboots until manually removed.", "first_seen": "2026-11-14T02:23:41+0100"}
